  "unreplied": [
    {
      "message_id": 149499,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8748487163",
      "user_name": "Cobalt",
      "time": "2026-04-28T15:34:50+00:00",
      "preview": "The massive floating magenta barathu, several kind and calm librarian's cadences in their telepathy, sparks internally and replies: \"We are no pirates, of this we can assure you. A mix of academics, warriors, and people of noble intention off to see to a dear comrade's request! You, dear, seem similarly not of the cutthroat's nature, though we have been wrong before... We are soon to reclaim this ship from the bellicose forces that surround our circumstances should you find yourself wishing to j",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149501,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Christopher",
      "time": "2026-04-28T15:47:37+00:00",
      "preview": "Her stance relaxes slightly, though there is no change in her expression or tone of voice. \"My name is Hinata Hoshibi. I would indeed like to join forces, as I am suffering from a distinct lack of allies on this hostile vessel. Though I would advise you to not shoot me in the back. I have eyes there as well. I excel at melee combat, the use of this fine weapon as well as the grouping together of enemies. I will answer less important questions later, once we can afford that luxury.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149511,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8748487163",
      "user_name": "Cobalt",
      "time": "2026-04-28T15:58:29+00:00",
      "preview": "Kae-Vo floats up a bit and excitedly waves their tendrils. \u201cEyes in the back of your head? Fascinating! Is that common for your species? Would you describe it as a useful adaptation to have? Are they more of photoreceptors or can you see in color with them? Is it something vestigial or more of a emergent trait? Are the number of eyes you possess correlated with the number of thumbs? We are often looking out for useful adaptations with which to alter our genetic sequence!\u201d",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149512,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8748487163",
      "user_name": "Cobalt",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:01:42+00:00",
      "preview": "\u201cAh, wait. This could be metaphor, based on your keen perception and past experience with betrayal at the hands of whom you once trusted. Forgive us if this has been an embarrassing outburst\u2026\u201d",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149513,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Christopher",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:13:17+00:00",
      "preview": "Hinata looks around in a manner that looks odd, as she seems to be looking for danger on only one of her flanks, but then, once she sees no immediate danger, turns around so that Kae-Vo can see the pair of eyes in the back of her head, around which her hair is styled to not obscure their vision.\n\"Yes, they are very useful to have. They work like my frontal eye pair and are common for my species, same with the additional number of thumbs. Well, at least for half of my parentage. I'm a half-blood.",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149514,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "7863964681",
      "user_name": "Link",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:20:05+00:00",
      "preview": "Joo-Dee, although entertained by the overall conversation, more or less steps in. \"As much as I value comradery, our ship is in the middle of a space battle between pirates and zombies, maybe we can bookmark this conversation until after we get out of here?\" She gives them her patented awkward glance and nudges her head in the direction of the access to the missile.",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149519,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "7863964681",
      "user_name": "Link",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:33:29+00:00",
      "preview": "\"Yeah,\" Joo-Dee interjects, \"we need to get this missile thing sorted, reclaim our ship, and then we can join hands in kumbaya.\"\nShe turns to the new arrival, curious on how she got here. Perhaps she escaped from the pirate ship, but pushes the though away. \n\"Hinata, nice to meet you. I'm Joo-Dee, you've spoken to Kae-Vo, we also have Holis, Chik, Arktos, Damon, and Oofy,\" She says, indicating each member.",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149521,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Christopher",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:36:24+00:00",
      "preview": "\"Nice to meet you as well. What can I do to help? My expertise lies mostly in combat and social matters, though I am also quite strong.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149523,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8748487163",
      "user_name": "Cobalt",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:40:47+00:00",
      "preview": "\u201cIn our defense.\u201d The telepathy is even softer than normal, as if the Symposium is murmuring to themselves under their psychic breath. The Symposium gently curls in their front tendrils to their body and spark blues and purples. \u201cThere is nothing to do except gathering data on those present until Chik and Arktos dislodge the missiles\u2026\u201d",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149524,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "7863964681",
      "user_name": "Link",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:42:35+00:00",
      "preview": "\"You comfortable with disarming missiles?\" Joo-Dee jests as she more or less tries to 'shoo' Arktos and Chik towards their next task.\n\nShe turns towards Kae-Vo, her voice tinged with guilt. \"I understand, just trying to keep our distractions to a minimum. Sorry for being harsh.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149537,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Christopher",
      "time": "2026-04-28T16:46:18+00:00",
      "preview": "She shakes her head. \"I am afraid that technical matters beyond the operation of guns are beyond my capabilities.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 149577,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8117756377",
      "user_name": "Laetheron",
      "time": "2026-04-28T19:28:28+00:00",
      "preview": "Arktos takes a brief moment to set their pack aside, entrusting it to LUKA. Then, adjusting their toolbelt, they clip Chik's cable to the back of their belt. And heads off through the magnetic field. \n\nAfter a few precarious teeters, Arktos manages their way to the missiles and begins tinkering.",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150136,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Christopher",
      "time": "2026-05-02T08:18:23+00:00",
      "preview": "Hinata looks between Joo-Dee and Kae-Vo. \"Since we will be fighting together, what can I expect of this group? Both in regards to capabilities and tactics.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150205,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "7863964681",
      "user_name": "Link",
      "time": "2026-05-02T13:53:57+00:00",
      "preview": "Joo-dee almost bursts into laughter as she recalls her recent encounters, but manages to keep her posture. \"Well, we killed the guy guarding our cell with out weapons that they put in the storage compartment underneath the cell. He lasted all but one shot. We then came across four of them a little while ago. Didn't take even ten seconds to dispatch them.\"\n\nShe shakes her head, \"honestly, it's extremely embarrassing that they managed to take the ship from us. Definitely going to have to work on a",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150217,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Chris Warlock",
      "time": "2026-05-02T15:30:14+00:00",
      "preview": "\"I see. So how did they take the ship from you?\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150331,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "7863964681",
      "user_name": "Link",
      "time": "2026-05-02T23:40:11+00:00",
      "preview": "\"We got knocked out by a high frequency sound wave. Didn't originated from the pirates it seems.",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150343,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Chris Warlock",
      "time": "2026-05-02T23:49:21+00:00",
      "preview": "\"Not much you could have done, it seems. We need to find whoever is wielding such a potent weapon and defeat them without giving them a chance to use it again.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    },
    {
      "message_id": 150762,
      "thread_id": 107171,
      "user_id": "8787586972",
      "user_name": "Chris Warlock",
      "time": "2026-05-03T14:12:37+00:00",
      "preview": "Hinata steps forward. \"What needs to be done? I have no technical knowledge, but I have strength and I can manipulate light and gravity to a degree.\"",
      "media_group_id": null
    }
  ],
